{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/archive/collection/abstraction-at-johnson-atelier","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":null,"type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"accession number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355"}],"content":"MS.65","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Abstraction at Johnson Atelier","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eGift of Betsy Bowen.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Related Material","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/relatedmaterial"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eExistence of additional related materials in the Seward Johnson Atelier archives.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eGeorgia O'Keeffe Abstraction Photographs (MS.15 / RC.2010.2) and Abstraction on Johnson Atelier Truck (MS.67 / 2022.7) are located at the Georgia O'Keeffe Museum.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD arrangement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/arrangement"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eCollection is arranged into two series: Photographic material and Articles.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"abstract","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/abstract"}],"content":"The collection consists of photographic materials and articles related to the creation of Georgia O'Keeffe's Abstraction sculpture at the Johnson Atelier Technical Institute of Sculpture. Photographs depict apprentices Betsy Bowen and Jacquie Bresadola posing with the unfinished sculptures, and Georgia O'Keeffe with co-executive directors Herk van Tongeren and Ron Young at Johnson Atelier with Abstraction. Materials date from 1978-1982.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Preferred Citation","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/prefercite"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eAbstraction at Johnson Atelier, 1978-1982, undated. Georgia O'Keeffe Museum.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Access restriction statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/accessrestrict"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eThe collection is open to the public for research purposes. Born-digital materials require advanced notice to ensure availability of equipment.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Restrictions on use","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/userestrict"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eCopies may be made for research purposes only.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Biographical Historical statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/bioghist"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eJ. Seward Johnson Jr. founded the Johnson Atelier Technical Institute of Sculpture (Princeton, NJ) in 1974 as a casting and fabrication facility with an emphasis on education. As such, the Institute had a robust apprenticeship program for hands-on learning as well as strong inclinations to experiment with new methods and techniques, working directly with sculptors to achieve their desired artistic outcome. Georgia O'Keeffe worked with the Johnson Atelier for the casting of her sculpture, Abstraction.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Acquisition information","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/acqinfo"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eThis collection was donated to the Georgia O'Keeffe Museum by Betsy Bowen in 2022.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Processing Information","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/processinfo"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eThis collection was processed by Ashley Baranyk in 2022.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Legal status statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/userestrict"}],"content":"This collection is the physical property of the Georgia O'Keeffe Museum. The Museum holds rights only for material created by Museum personnel or given to the Museum with such rights specifically assigned. The collection is subject to all copyright laws. The researcher assumes full responsibility for observing all copyright, property, and libel laws as they apply. Contact the Archivist for further copyright and publication information as it pertains to this collection.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}